10
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Self - Investigative Journalist for The Guardian, played by Carole Cadwalladr.

11
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
The Great Hack is a 2019 documentary film about the Facebook–Cambridge Analytica data scandal, produced and directed by Jehane
Noujaim and Karim Amer, both previous documentary Academy Award nominees (The Square, Control Room, Startup.com).

12
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film's music was composed by Emmy-nominated film composer Gil Talmi.

13
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
The Great Hack premiered at the 2019 Sundance Film Festival in the Documentary
Premieres section and was released by Netflix on July 24, 2019.

14
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
The documentary focuses on David Carroll of Parsons and The New School, Brittany Kaiser (former business
development director for Cambridge Analytica), and British investigative journalist Carole Cadwalladr.

15
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
Their stories interweave to expose the work of Cambridge Analytica in the politics of various
countries, including the United Kingdom's Brexit campaign and the 2016 United States elections.

16
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
The film explores themes of propaganda, politics, united
kingdom, social network, behavior modification.

17
01:47:40,000 --> 01:47:46,000
The tone is dark.
